        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(tlon): cap SSE payload JSON.parse at 16 MiB to prevent OOM",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`parseUrbitSsePayload()` and `processStream()` in `extensions/tlon/src/urbit/sse-client.ts` have two unbounded memory paths on external Urbit ship SSE data:\n\n1. **Stream buffer accumulation** (primary): `processStream` appends chunks into `buffer` with no byte cap. A hostile ship can send an unterminated SSE event (no `\\n\\n`) and exhaust memory before any event is dispatched.\n2. **JSON.parse** (defense-in-depth): `parseUrbitSsePayload` calls `JSON.parse(data)` with no size limit, allowing a large single event to OOM.\n\nBoth paths are now capped at 16 MiB, matching the merged pattern in `extensions/signal/src/client.ts` (bounded SSE buffer + bounded event data).\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- **Stream buffer**: Added incremental `Buffer.byteLength` tracking in `processStream`. Each chunk's byte-length is accumulated; if total exceeds 16 MiB, the stream is rejected before memory exhaustion.\n- **Parse guard**: Retained as defense-in-depth — oversized events that slip through the stream cap (e.g., `\\n\\n`-delimited but individual event data > 16 MiB) are still rejected at parse time.\n\nPattern aligned with Signal SSE (`extensions/signal/src/client.ts:36-37`, `MAX_SIGNAL_SSE_BUFFER_BYTES` / `MAX_SIGNAL_SSE_EVENT_DATA_BYTES`) and the 16 MiB constants used across `extensions/google/`, `extensions/feishu/`, `extensions/xai/`, etc.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Normal SSE events processed unchanged\n- Stream buffer exceeding 16 MiB: logged + stream error handler invoked + auto-reconnect\n- No change to malformed JSON handling or small-event behavior\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Bug exists on main** (b1da734a1e): both `processStream` (unbounded `buffer +=`) and `parseUrbitSsePayload` (raw `JSON.parse`) lack size guards\n- **No competing PR**: full search across `parseUrbitSsePayload`, `sse-client`, tlon+SSE, unbounded+OOM — 0 open PRs touch this path\n- **Tests**: 21/21 passed locally, including 3 stream-path tests:\n  - oversized 17 × 1 MiB chunks without `\\n\\n` → rejected at buffer cap\n  - normal `\\n\\n`-delimited event → handler receives `{ok: true}`\n  - 1000 small events → all delivered, buffer trim path exercised\n- **CI**: force-push re-triggered; the `checks-node-compact-small-whole-2` failure in the initial run was a flake\n\n```\nOPENCLAW_VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=1 node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/tlon/src/urbit/sse-client.test.ts\nTests: 21 passed (21)\n```",
        "branch": "fix/tlon-sse-bounded-json-parse",
